Alternative: A stronger functional test — use Chromium's headless with `--repl`? Not available in new headless. Could add a temporary debug hook: temporarily append to game a `window.__stats = ...` — but I don't want to ship debug code. Option: run a separate test copy (test.html) = index.html + injected instrumentation script that after N seconds fills document.title with state (autopilot, asteroid count, score>0). Then dump-dom and grep title. Autopilot takes time to shoot asteroids; with faster virtual time hard to control. Alternative instrumentation: expose getters and use setInterval to write into DOM. Since `--timeout` based screenshot previously waited 12s real-time, the AI had 12s to play; score HUD may have advanced. Let me analyze the score corner of the screenshot: crop top-left 300x60 and OCR-ish check? No OCR. But bright pixel count in score region indicates text; can't read digits.

