Wait — asteroid array is `const asteroids=[]` global lexical — accessible ✓. `state` is `let` ✓. But at the time the interval fires, if AI shot asteroids, score > 0. After 12s of demo, AI should have destroyed several asteroids (they start large, AI leads shots decently). Let's run with --timeout=15000 and --dump-dom... Actually new headless `--dump-dom --timeout` — dump after timeout? --dump-dom dumps after page load completes (load event), not after timeout necessarily. Hmm: In headless mode, --dump-dom prints DOM of the page to stdout. With --timeout it waits for that before dumping? Chrome docs: "--timeout: Issues shutdown after the timeout so that slow-loading pages... " The timeout makes headless wait? From Chromium usage: `--timeout=N` (in ms) gives the page N ms to load/run before acting. I believe dump-dom acts at load event OR timeout, whichever... The earlier screenshot with --timeout=12000 produced a 12s-later screenshot presumably (and exit=0). I think --timeout delays the action until post-load timeout expires. Good.

